# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Evaluated top to bottom; first match wins.
#
# Pages serves `build.format: 'file'` output at extensionless URLs natively, so
# /work resolves to work.html with no rule here. What this file is for is the
# URLs that existed BEFORE this build: §8's rule is that old URLs 301, never 404.
#
# PROJECT: replace the examples below with the real old surface. The way to
# produce that list is to export every indexed URL from Search Console and the
# old CMS, not to guess — a 404 on an indexed URL is lost ranking, and the only
# way to know which ones exist is to look.
#
# Every line here is commented out. An empty _redirects file is correct for a new
# site; a file full of redirects to pages that do not exist is not.

# --- Pages that moved ------------------------------------------------------
# /about                 /company                301
# /old-blog/:slug        /writing/:slug          301

# --- Trailing-slash normalisation ------------------------------------------
# `trailingSlash: 'never'` in astro.config.mjs, so a slashed URL should 301
# rather than serve a duplicate.
# /work/                 /work                   301
# /contact/              /contact                301

# --- .html suffix → canonical extensionless --------------------------------
# For anything linked or bookmarked with the extension.
# /index.html            /                       301
# /work.html             /work                   301

# --- Retired sections ------------------------------------------------------
# Point at the nearest useful page, never at the home page by default: a 301 to
# / tells a crawler the content is gone and tells a visitor nothing.
# /services/legacy-thing /services               301
